# Generated outputs
output/*
!output/.gitkeep
thirdparty/
.worktrees/

# Bun's compile scratch. `bun build --compile` writes `.<hash>-<n>.bun-build` in the repo root with mode
# 000 and removes it on success, so it is only ever visible when a build is interrupted. Untracked and
# unignored, it entered `git ls-files --others --exclude-standard` and hard-crashed both check-public-tree
# and the source fingerprint on EACCES — two required gates felled by a killed build. The pattern covers
# every `.bun-build` name, not just the dot-prefixed one Bun happens to emit today: the gate crash is a
# property of the extension, and a leading-dot rule would let a renamed scratch file fell the gate again.
*.bun-build

